API-22: reduce API time-of-day control times modulo 24 hours

The input-file parser reduces a CLOCKTIME control time modulo 86400 s,
so "CLOCKTIME 24:00" means midnight. setcontrol(), used by
EN_addcontrol and EN_setcontrol, stored the time as given. The solver
compares it with the clock time of day, which is always under 86400 s,
so a time of 24 h or more never fired. Reduce it the same way.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-22_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/project.c b/src/project.c
index 792ccab..8b89c41 100644
--- a/src/project.c
+++ b/src/project.c
@@ -1379,6 +1379,7 @@ int setcontrol(EN_Project p, int type, int linkIndex, double setting,
     {
         t = (long)level;
         if (t < 0) return 202;
+        if (type == TIMEOFDAY) t %= SECperDAY;
     }
     
     // Assign values to control struct
